# Intent: Draws the new ICON shape (patch GM04): each icon is a table of rounded boxes, discs, rings and thick lines in a 100 by 100 grid laid out from LVGL objects (at most 6 boxes or discs and 4 lines), so one routine draws every icon at every size; an icon whose number is fixed allocates only its own parts. A popping icon grows from half size with an overshoot in 300 ms when it appears (Do It's action, the two hands of Rock Paper Scissors) and a bumping icon (the counting fist) rises and falls once for each state entered. The see-through fill and the 24 px text size are drawn. The old hand-placed motion code for Rock Paper Scissors (hands that bump, the unit's pick fading in) and for Do It's called tile pulse is removed: both games are built from icons now. Still pictures taken by the host renderer are taken after the pop, never in the middle of it.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_games_draw.h (ours, UI13, UI15, GM02)
# Check after a flash: In Do It the icon pops when the action is shown; in Rock Paper Scissors the fist bumps with each beat and both hands pop at the reveal.
# Kconfig: none

